1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,100
[The content, events, techniques, and outcomes of massage
depicted in this series]

2
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:08,211
[are entirely fictional and intended for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,421
[They should not be used as medical advice or as a reference
for traditional Thai massage.]

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,901
[Viewer discretion is advised. Do not attempt to imitate
any of the techniques shown,]

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,001
[as doing so may result in injury.]

6
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:13,161
[Massage services should only be provided by practitioners]

7
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:14,900
[who are legally licensed and registered.]

8
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,800
- What about Phat?
- That boy?

9
00:00:17,062 --> 00:00:18,063
I'll take care of him myself.

10
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:20,890
If you find Hattha and her family, kill them all.

11
00:00:20,901 --> 00:00:22,760
- Muk?-
- Master Tim wants to talk to you two.

12
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,000
Especially Hattha.

13
00:00:24,272 --> 00:00:25,280
Those bruises on your neck...

14
00:00:25,366 --> 00:00:26,367
Master Tim did that to you, didn't he?

15
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:27,800
Get in the car!

16
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,080
- Hey.
- If you don't run now, I won't be able to help you anymore.

17
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:31,091
Thank you.

18
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:32,840
You did all this

19
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,840
just because I was that little girl?

20
00:00:35,043 --> 00:00:37,440
You were the last bit of happiness in my life.

21
00:00:37,928 --> 00:00:39,729
It's too late for me to turn my life around.

22
00:00:39,784 --> 00:00:41,200
But you can still stop now.

23
00:00:41,214 --> 00:00:42,560
Stop looking for that flatfooted bastard.

24
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,600
And go back to living your life with your dad.

25
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,301
Thank you for letting me know.

26
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:50,240
Let's go.

27
00:00:50,347 --> 00:00:51,440
He did the right thing.

28
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:52,801
Wan.

29
00:00:53,406 --> 00:00:54,640
- What?
- That's Mr. Krit.

30
00:00:54,899 --> 00:00:56,400
I know who can help us.

31
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,472
Hey! Wait.

32
00:01:08,534 --> 00:01:09,920
Flatfoot insoles?

33
00:01:10,203 --> 00:01:11,440
Mr. Krit uses these too?

34
00:02:11,691 --> 00:02:13,640
- Beat the shit out of him.
- Yes, boss.

35
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:14,767
Hey, let's do this!

36
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:18,040
Hey! Get my shoe.

37
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:22,511
Let's go!

38
00:02:33,952 --> 00:02:35,040
Mr. Krit has flat feet.

39
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,441
[Master Tim sent a photo.]

40
00:03:05,451 --> 00:03:06,452
Why did you take my dad?

41
00:03:06,939 --> 00:03:09,240
I sent someone to bring you here nicely. Why didn't you come?

42
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,361
What do you want?

43
00:03:12,758 --> 00:03:14,600
Your father's deadly massage manual.

44
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,071
In exchange for his life.

45
00:03:20,459 --> 00:03:22,120
How are my dad and Uncle Korn doing?

46
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,501
Let me talk to them.

47
00:03:24,083 --> 00:03:25,240
You're really worried about them, huh?

48
00:03:26,088 --> 00:03:27,880
Then you'd better hurry up and get here.

49
00:03:29,406 --> 00:03:31,250
I'm not a patient man, you know.

50
00:03:37,875 --> 00:03:39,080
The deadly massage manual?

51
00:03:41,107 --> 00:03:42,712
But Uncle Korn already burned the notebook.

52
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:44,480
He said it was unreadable, too.

53
00:03:45,931 --> 00:03:47,200
Then what are you going to give Master Tim?

54
00:03:47,494 --> 00:03:48,880
I'll have to use that manual.

55
00:03:49,678 --> 00:03:52,040
I kept it in a bag I was taking to the house in Photharam.

56
00:03:53,126 --> 00:03:54,127
Then let's go.

57
00:03:59,984 --> 00:04:01,040
Wan, you'll have to go alone.

58
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:06,240
- Why?
- I have something to take care of.

59
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:09,707
Wait, what else do you have to do?

60
00:04:10,811 --> 00:04:12,054
I saw Mr. Krit attacking Phat.

61
00:04:13,928 --> 00:04:14,929
Be careful.

62
00:04:16,702 --> 00:04:17,703
Keep me posted.

63
00:04:48,096 --> 00:04:50,000
Phat! Phat!

64
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,521
Get up! Get up!

65
00:04:55,472 --> 00:04:56,473
One, two.

66
00:04:59,483 --> 00:05:00,484
What's wrong? Can't breathe?

67
00:05:01,974 --> 00:05:03,000
Come here.

68
00:05:03,014 --> 00:05:04,027
Got the wind knocked out of you? Come here.

69
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,560
Phat, lift your head. Lift it up.

70
00:05:11,363 --> 00:05:12,480
Slowly lower it.

71
00:05:12,702 --> 00:05:13,960
Slowly lower it.

72
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,001
Okay.

73
00:05:16,867 --> 00:05:17,868
Lift your head.

74
00:05:19,176 --> 00:05:20,177
Lift your head.

75
00:05:20,531 --> 00:05:22,520
Okay, now slowly lower it.

76
00:05:25,128 --> 00:05:26,129
Lift your head.

77
00:05:27,656 --> 00:05:28,657
Slowly lower it.

78
00:05:33,582 --> 00:05:34,583
Lift your head.

79
00:05:38,278 --> 00:05:39,279
Slowly lower it.

80
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,561
Phat.

81
00:05:47,947 --> 00:05:49,320
Can you get up? Let's get you to the hospital. Come on.

82
00:05:50,771 --> 00:05:51,772
No.

83
00:05:51,810 --> 00:05:52,811
I'm not going to the hospital.

84
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,741
Take me to my room.

85
00:05:59,790 --> 00:06:01,240
Phat, wait.

86
00:06:02,248 --> 00:06:03,320
Come here.

87
00:06:26,454 --> 00:06:28,480
Why did Mr. Krit attack you?

88
00:06:35,504 --> 00:06:38,440
He's Dongyang's business partner.

89
00:06:44,747 --> 00:06:46,779
Is there anyone who actually cares about this country?

90
00:06:53,792 --> 00:06:55,360
Then why didn't he kill you?

91
00:07:02,875 --> 00:07:03,876
I don't know.

92
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,136
Maybe because I'm still useful to him.

93
00:07:13,686 --> 00:07:16,270
Get some rest. I'll go get you some medicine.

94
00:07:25,835 --> 00:07:26,836
Go lie down.

95
00:07:57,779 --> 00:07:58,810
Stop it, Minkheng.

96
00:08:00,486 --> 00:08:01,720
They brought us all the way here.

97
00:08:02,363 --> 00:08:03,764
They're not going to let us go that easily.

98
00:08:18,523 --> 00:08:19,840
You haven't changed a bit, In.

99
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:22,800
But you've changed a lot.

100
00:08:26,168 --> 00:08:27,200
Just wait a little longer.

101
00:08:30,078 --> 00:08:31,160
Your daughter will be here soon.

102
00:08:32,152 --> 00:08:33,360
What are you going to do to my daughter?

103
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:36,640
Just make her bring me the deadly massage manual.

104
00:08:38,702 --> 00:08:40,400
The deadly massage manual?

105
00:08:41,834 --> 00:08:44,960
I asked you to help me find a way.

106
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:48,720
But when you found it,

107
00:08:50,264 --> 00:08:51,865
you kept it all to yourself.

108
00:08:52,403 --> 00:08:55,120
Fine, I admit I lied to you.

109
00:08:56,136 --> 00:08:57,840
Because I didn't want a technique like this

110
00:08:58,303 --> 00:09:00,280
to fall into the hands of someone like you.

111
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:04,041
What's wrong with someone like me?

112
00:09:05,691 --> 00:09:06,920
What's so bad about me?

113
00:09:11,969 --> 00:09:12,970
Tell me!

114
00:09:14,171 --> 00:09:15,880
I've already burned that manual.

115
00:09:17,467 --> 00:09:18,760
It was unreadable anyway.

116
00:09:20,176 --> 00:09:21,500
Even if you've burned it,

117
00:09:23,403 --> 00:09:25,704
you still have to teach me how to do it.

118
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:30,000
Until I can kill someone with massage.

119
00:09:31,216 --> 00:09:32,217
Understand?

120
00:09:36,512 --> 00:09:38,610
Tim, it's been so many years.

121
00:09:39,019 --> 00:09:41,460
- Are you still obsessed with it?
- Shut your mouth!

122
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:44,280
And you! You helped him keep it from me.

123
00:09:44,507 --> 00:09:45,680
You even helped him go into hiding.

124
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,680
If you weren't my brother,

125
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:49,381
I would've dealt with you and your son long ago.

126
00:09:57,998 --> 00:09:59,000
Now that's more like

127
00:10:00,622 --> 00:10:02,952
the same old asshole brother I know.

128
00:10:11,923 --> 00:10:12,924
Let go of me!

129
00:10:19,256 --> 00:10:20,257
Stop it right now!

130
00:10:20,808 --> 00:10:22,700
I'll do whatever you want! Just stop!

131
00:10:23,347 --> 00:10:24,348
Stop!

132
00:10:30,507 --> 00:10:31,920
- Muk!
- Yes?

133
00:10:32,102 --> 00:10:33,103
Keep an eye on them.

134
00:10:34,502 --> 00:10:36,120
Don't screw up like last time.

135
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,601
How are you, Inn?

136
00:10:42,147 --> 00:10:43,148
I'm okay.

137
00:10:46,827 --> 00:10:48,120
This deadly massage technique...

138
00:10:49,238 --> 00:10:50,360
Does it really work?

139
00:11:14,579 --> 00:11:17,000
Hello, Muk. This is Wan.

140
00:11:17,219 --> 00:11:18,520
I got your number from Ya.

141
00:11:19,288 --> 00:11:21,400
Master Tim has kidnapped my dad,

142
00:11:21,566 --> 00:11:23,440
Uncle Korn, and Minkheng.

143
00:11:23,646 --> 00:11:25,582
Have you seen them? Are they okay?

144
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:29,080
Yes, everyone's still safe.

145
00:11:31,752 --> 00:11:33,155
If you want them all to survive,

146
00:11:33,635 --> 00:11:35,512
you need to bring Master Tim the deadly massage manual.

147
00:11:36,227 --> 00:11:37,240
That's all I can say.

148
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,081
[Do Not Read]

149
00:12:37,782 --> 00:12:40,720
At least we know Master Tim won't hurt Dad and the others.

150
00:12:41,646 --> 00:12:43,379
So what's your plan?

151
00:12:44,216 --> 00:12:46,600
Why did you ask me to get this unreadable manual?

152
00:12:47,198 --> 00:12:49,000
We still need the original manual as proof.

153
00:12:49,611 --> 00:12:50,612
But I've memorized the whole thing.

154
00:12:51,387 --> 00:12:52,742
I'm writing a new one.

155
00:12:54,326 --> 00:12:55,584
Then we'll go see Master Tim together.

156
00:12:58,342 --> 00:12:59,760
How's Phat doing?

157
00:13:00,862 --> 00:13:02,307
He tried to kill Dongyang, but he's still alive.

158
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:04,751
I think you should be careful around him.

159
00:13:07,214 --> 00:13:08,215
I am keeping an eye on him.

160
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,521
I want to know the truth, too.

161
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:13,880
Something feels off to me.

162
00:13:14,646 --> 00:13:16,000
None of it adds up.

163
00:13:16,294 --> 00:13:18,040
He's Dongyang's bodyguard,

164
00:13:18,763 --> 00:13:20,440
but he's risked his life to save you several times.

165
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,430
And after doing something that serious, he's still alive.

166
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,111
Mom?

167
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,901
- No!
- Wan, I have to go.

168
00:13:36,312 --> 00:13:37,313
Don't leave me.

169
00:13:42,328 --> 00:13:43,329
Phat?

170
00:13:47,774 --> 00:13:48,840
- Mom!
- Phat!

171
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,321
Don't leave me.

172
00:13:50,408 --> 00:13:51,409
Phat.

173
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:53,921
Mom.

174
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,441
[Flatfoot]

175
00:17:00,526 --> 00:17:01,527
Feeling better already?

176
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,441
A little better.

177
00:17:03,779 --> 00:17:05,100
So I went out to get some food.

178
00:17:13,088 --> 00:17:14,400
Then why did you buy a plant?

179
00:17:15,766 --> 00:17:17,100
I'm going to plant it in the garden.

180
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,401
Come with me.

181
00:17:28,056 --> 00:17:29,640
How did I end up sleeping in bed?

182
00:17:33,328 --> 00:17:35,846
Maybe you sleepwalked there.

183
00:17:37,329 --> 00:17:38,330
I was asleep.

184
00:17:41,475 --> 00:17:42,476
Want some?

185
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:44,160
I'll go take a shower first.

186
00:18:00,182 --> 00:18:01,600
Oh, Uncle!

187
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:03,700
- Hello, Phat.
- Hello.

188
00:18:03,811 --> 00:18:05,840
Here, I brought you some snacks.

189
00:18:06,339 --> 00:18:07,720
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

190
00:18:07,907 --> 00:18:09,600
There was a storm the other day.

191
00:18:09,822 --> 00:18:12,200
It knocked down a bunch of our trees.

192
00:18:12,568 --> 00:18:14,120
I've got everything ready.

193
00:18:14,302 --> 00:18:16,302
I'll stop by and take a look after work.

194
00:18:16,526 --> 00:18:18,000
It's okay. I'll take care of it myself.

195
00:18:18,211 --> 00:18:19,960
- Thank you. See you later.
- See ya.

196
00:18:20,062 --> 00:18:21,063
Enjoy the snacks.

197
00:18:41,486 --> 00:18:42,560
Why do you plant trees?

198
00:18:49,971 --> 00:18:51,120
Every tree I plant

199
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,160
represents a life.

200
00:19:02,283 --> 00:19:03,480
That was the first one.

201
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,100
The day I completed my first job,

202
00:19:09,926 --> 00:19:11,327
I came home and couldn't sleep.

203
00:19:12,624 --> 00:19:15,080
My uncle scolded me. He said if I wanted to do this for a living,

204
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,200
I'd have to learn to live with it.

205
00:19:37,427 --> 00:19:38,760
So that's why you started planting trees?

206
00:19:39,752 --> 00:19:41,240
I know it can't make up for what I've done.

207
00:19:43,384 --> 00:19:45,960
But at least it makes me feel like I'm making amends somehow.

208
00:20:01,643 --> 00:20:03,044
What was your first time like?

209
00:20:09,779 --> 00:20:11,144
What happened to me doesn't matter.

210
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:15,600
But I don't want you to end up like me.

211
00:20:18,656 --> 00:20:20,200
Stop looking for Flatfoot.

212
00:20:22,331 --> 00:20:24,000
Are you worried about me or someone else?

213
00:20:28,512 --> 00:20:30,203
And the day Mr. Krit attacked you,

214
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:32,320
what did he say to you?

215
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:37,200
He was furious that I killed Dongyang.

216
00:20:47,515 --> 00:20:48,720
Was all of this because of me?

217
00:20:55,702 --> 00:20:56,703
Phat.

218
00:20:59,568 --> 00:21:01,440
I'm sorry. I won't cause you any more trouble.

219
00:21:03,078 --> 00:21:04,280
What are you planning to do now?

220
00:21:34,555 --> 00:21:36,880
From now on, Master Tim and I

221
00:21:37,312 --> 00:21:40,330
will be taking over Arokaya Land from Dongyang.

222
00:21:41,536 --> 00:21:42,537
Don't worry.

223
00:21:43,675 --> 00:21:45,080
Even though Dongyang is gone,

224
00:21:45,499 --> 00:21:47,240
all our deals will remain unchanged.

225
00:21:47,910 --> 00:21:49,734
There's still no progress in Dongyang's case.

226
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,112
And you're making an announcement like this?

227
00:21:54,150 --> 00:21:56,051
I can't help but think

228
00:21:58,246 --> 00:21:59,720
Phat was just a bodyguard.

229
00:22:00,544 --> 00:22:03,160
He wouldn't have dared do it unless someone ordered him to.

230
00:22:05,291 --> 00:22:06,960
Nobody ordered him to do anything.

231
00:22:07,686 --> 00:22:10,280
The autopsy report confirmed it was an accident.

232
00:22:10,736 --> 00:22:12,240
Dongyang fell down the stairs.

233
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,541
So that's how you want to play it?

234
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:20,000
Actually, I think this is a good thing.

235
00:22:20,467 --> 00:22:22,446
Because we finally get to meet face-to-face.

236
00:22:22,856 --> 00:22:25,304
No more dealing through a nominee like Dongyang.

237
00:22:26,104 --> 00:22:28,320
Now we can make decisions directly.

238
00:22:28,579 --> 00:22:30,920
Why worry about someone who's already dead?

239
00:22:32,131 --> 00:22:34,760
Wouldn't it be better to work together on our next project?

240
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,840
Shouldn't we focus on what we stand to gain?

241
00:22:38,256 --> 00:22:40,925
Is that why you got rid of Brother Yang?

242
00:22:41,552 --> 00:22:44,614
You and Master Tim are trying to take over his business, aren't you?

243
00:23:02,523 --> 00:23:04,379
I've been more than generous.

244
00:23:05,958 --> 00:23:06,959
Now,

245
00:23:08,214 --> 00:23:09,215
what's it going to be?

246
00:23:18,904 --> 00:23:19,905
Deal.

247
00:23:21,512 --> 00:23:22,513
That's more like it.

248
00:23:24,627 --> 00:23:26,320
There are so many reporters here.

249
00:23:26,590 --> 00:23:27,760
Hey, here he comes!

250
00:23:28,950 --> 00:23:31,680
- Sir, could we have an interview?
- Could we ask you a few questions?

251
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,131
Could we have an interview, please?

252
00:23:33,232 --> 00:23:34,280
Could we interview you, sir?

253
00:23:35,254 --> 00:23:37,400
There were earlier reports that Dongyang was ill.

254
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:39,301
So how did he suddenly pass away?

255
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:41,160
It was an accident.

256
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:44,400
Dongyang fell down the stairs at his place.

257
00:23:45,041 --> 00:23:46,642
We were just as shocked by the news.

258
00:23:46,835 --> 00:23:49,400
Will this affect the Arokaya project?

259
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,001
No, it won't.

260
00:23:51,310 --> 00:23:53,360
The project will continue as planned.

261
00:23:54,158 --> 00:23:57,759
Master Tim will take over from Dongyang.

262
00:23:58,792 --> 00:24:00,078
But there's no need to worry.

263
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,590
Even though we're both Thai,

264
00:24:02,872 --> 00:24:06,280
I'll be conducting even stricter inspections.

265
00:24:06,704 --> 00:24:10,520
So I'd like to apologize to Master Tim in advance.

266
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,440
Of course. No problem at all.

267
00:24:13,803 --> 00:24:15,560
And my commitment

268
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:20,120
to promoting Thai massage as a form of soft power

269
00:24:20,568 --> 00:24:22,611
and making it famous around the world, as I've often said,

270
00:24:23,155 --> 00:24:24,156
